config MODULE_GATE
	bool "ModuleGate: audit and gate kernel module loads"
	default y
	depends on SECURITY && CRYPTO_SHA256
	help
	  Tiny LSM hooking kernel_post_load_data() for LOADING_MODULE --
	  the single choke point every insmod/modprobe/init/autoload path
	  converges on (finit_module). Decisions are made on the SHA256 of
	  the actual module bytes, never on spoofable names.

	  Modes via /sys/kernel/module_gate/mode (default 0):
	    0 audit   - unknown hashes auto-enroll (TOFU), allowed, logged.
	    1 enforce - unknown hashes denied with -EPERM, logged, counted.
	  Boot phase (before SYSTEM_RUNNING) never enforces, so a wrong
	  list cannot brick boot; audit still records every load.

	  Fires once per module load (dozens at boot, ~zero after): no hot
	  path, no timers, no polling. List capped at 256 entries.
